<DocsLayout active="architecture" title="Architecture" description="A small service with an explicit privacy boundary: request, policy, detection, replacement, and audit.">
  <section><h2 class="text-[25px] text-ink-0">One boundary, five stages</h2><p class="mt-3">Redax runs next to your application. The API receives a request, applies a versioned policy, runs deterministic patterns first, optionally calls a local encoder, fuses overlapping spans, replaces selected spans, then writes only redaction metadata to the audit log.</p></section>
  <div class="code-shell overflow-x-auto p-6 font-mono text-[13px] leading-[1.9] text-ink-200"><pre><code>{`client → POST /v1/redact → policy → regex + model → consensus
       → typed replacement → safe text + spans + digest
                                      ↘ audit metadata only`}</code></pre></div>
  <section><h2 class="text-[25px] text-ink-0">Operational surfaces</h2><div class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">{[["/healthz", "Liveness"], ["/readyz", "Readiness"], ["/metrics", "Prometheus"], ["OTLP", "OpenTelemetry traces"]].map(([path, label]) => <div class="card p-5"><code class="text-flame-200">{path}</code><div class="mt-2 text-[14px] text-ink-300">{label}</div></div>)}</div></section>
  <section><h2 class="text-[25px] text-ink-0">What happens to one request</h2><ol class="mt-4 grid gap-3">{[["1. Authenticate", "The API key is checked when authentication is configured."], ["2. Admit", "Rate limits, request size, timeouts, and job capacity protect the service."], ["3. Detect", "The configured regex and model detectors produce candidate spans."], ["4. Apply", "Offsets are validated, overlaps are resolved, and the policy chooses the replacement."], ["5. Record", "The audit backend writes counts, types, duration, and request metadata—never values."], ["6. Respond", "The client receives safe text, spans, digest, and request correlation data."]].map(([title, body]) => <li class="card p-5 sm:flex sm:gap-5"><strong class="shrink-0 text-[14px] text-ink-0">{title}</strong><span class="mt-1 sm:mt-0 text-[14px] text-ink-400">{body}</span></li>)}</ol></section>
  <section><h2 class="text-[25px] text-ink-0">Why the pieces are separate</h2><p class="mt-3">Detection answers “where is sensitive text?” Policy answers “what should happen to it?” Replacement answers “what can the next system safely see?” Audit answers “how can we prove what happened without storing the secret?” Keeping those decisions separate makes a change reviewable and lets operators replace a detector without changing the privacy contract.</p></section>
  <section><h2 class="text-[25px] text-ink-0">What is deliberately absent</h2><p class="mt-3">The default model path does not call a hosted inference service. Redax does not promise that surrounding infrastructure is silent: configure your proxy, Redis, audit storage, model cache, and telemetry exporter as part of the deployment boundary you operate.</p></section>
</DocsLayout>
